# KNOWN GAP — LIVE MISCOMPILE AT CLEAN HEAD. `Box[T]` over PRIMITIVE element
# types collapses every unnamed element onto ONE `Box__int64_t` typedef, alloc
# helper and drop fn, whose body is generated by whichever type reached the mint
# FIRST. The later box then reads through the wrong layout.
#
#     Box[float] bf = Box[float](1.5)
#     Box[uint8] bu = Box[uint8](200)
#     print((*bf))    # 1.500000   correct
#     print((*bu))    # 0          WRONG -- 200 expected
#
# `gg check` rc 0, `gg build` rc 0, run rc 0. A wrong value is the ONLY symptom
# on the C backend. Symmetric on reverse declaration order. The LLVM lane hard-
# errors in `llc` on the identical program.
#
# ⚠ MECHANISM: `type_name_for_id` misses every primitive TypeId, so the mint at
# `src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs` falls through to `.unwrap_or("int64_t")`.
# The emitted C shows the collapse directly -- `Box__int64_t` appears beside
# `Box__double` and `Box__uint8_t`.
#
# ⚠ `Box.new` is CORRECT here: it uses `c_type_name_for_id`. That asymmetry is
# a third independent disproof of the comment claiming both entry points produce
# identical IR (Core #14).
#
# ⚠ This is NOT a hazard introduced by any in-flight fix -- it reproduces at
# clean HEAD with zero fixtures and zero prior filings covering it.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints 1.500000 then 200.
# Found 2026-08-27 by R45 Track A brief-review pass 2; orchestrator-verified.

void main():
    Box[float] bf = Box[float](1.5)
    Box[uint8] bu = Box[uint8](200)
    print((*bf))
    print((*bu))
